cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these patches, cite the trees they apply to.
title: cloth-fit dependency patches for fit.elf
abstract: >-
  Patches applied to pinned V-Sekai-fire forks of cloth-fit's CPM
  dependencies for the fit.elf build (Cut 6), kept as patch files so the
  fork pins stay the revisions cloth-fit's recipes name.
  polysolve-embedded-specs.patch applies to V-Sekai-fire/polysolve at
  ee553dc6 (branch garment, from Huangzizhou/polysolve): Solver::create in
  nonlinear/Solver.cpp, nonlinear/BoxConstraintSolver.cpp and
  linear/Solver.cpp read their JSON rules from absolute build-machine paths
  (POLYSOLVE_NON_LINEAR_SPEC, POLYSOLVE_LINEAR_SPEC); with the new CMake
  option POLYSOLVE_EMBEDDED_SPECS they take them from
  polysolve_embedded_spec(name), which the embedding program defines
  (tools/fit/embed_files.py over guest/fit/specs). Off, the library is
  unchanged. tools/fit/prepare_forks.sh applies it in the worktree
  .forks/polysolve-guest; .forks/polysolve stays unpatched for the oracle.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Zizhou Huang
  - name: The PolyFEM contributors
  - name: K. S. Ernest (iFire) Lee
  - name: V-Sekai
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/polysolve
